ANACREON 10
"The Four Princes"
0     ; random scenario
2 4   ; 2-4 players
30    ; 30x30 galaxy
63    ; 105 planets
1     ; Difficulty
20 30 ; 20-30 years
3501

BEGINTEXT


    "In the fourth millennium since the assassination of the Emperor the 
    Spinward Alliance set the pace for the sectors in the Tyreemean Arm. The 
    influence of its imperialist doctrines upon the minds of regional 
    governors throughout the area was particularly strong given the latter's 
    strong megalomaniac tendencies. The impulse to rise out of local 
    obscurity and wield control over inter-stellar affairs soon compelled 
    many governors to burst out of their territories and undertake a 
    systematic program of conquest and expansion. Dramatic as the emergence 
    of these states were, by far the greatest affect of the Spinward 
    influence was the rise of the Four Princes of Erewohl and the perpetual 
    wars which they waged in the Erewohl sector, not far from the old city 
    of Taskunee." 
                              - From: Catastrophe of Modern Imperialism
                                      by Lenoree de Sarima

NEWPAGE
ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

WorldBackgroundIndex
2:1 E:0          1     ; CloseUp: Empire 1 capital
2:6 E:1          2     ; CloseUp: Empire 2 capital
2:11 E:2         3     ; CloseUp: Empire 3 capital
2:15 E:3         4     ; CloseUp: Empire 4 capital
EndIndex

TEXT 1
History: As a trade center with contacts all the way to the Spinward 
Alliance, this world easily became the nucleus for a fledgeling empire in 
the Erewohl sector. In conflict with the other three princes of the 
sector, this empire can boast of a modern attack fleet with the most advanced 
ships.

Recommended Victory Conditions: Last surviving empire in the sector.
ENDTEXT 

TEXT 2
History: Although this world was nearly devastated by a series of nuclear 
accidents two centuries ago, it has now risen to command an empire of 
great military and industrial strength. The Imperial Starfleet of this 
empire is the largest of all the princes save the defensive central 
empire.

Recommended Victory Conditions: Last surviving empire in the sector.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 3
History: The youngest of the four empires, this world rose to power only 
in the last few years through the accidental discovery of an ancient 
industrial complex. Although is current military power is small compared 
to the other, its ship production is second to none.

Recommended Victory Conditions: Last surviving empire in the sector.
ENDTEXT

TEXT 4
History: The capital of the oldest empire in the Erewohl sector, this 
world was originally the sector headquarters for the Imperial Starfleet of 
the First Empire. After the rise of the Spinward Alliance, this world 
seceded to form its own empire. Although it is militarily the most 
powerful empire in the sector, most of its forces are defensive in nature.

Recommended Victory Conditions: Last surviving empire in the sector.
ENDTEXT

ENDDESCRIPTION

